WEBVTT

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:03.640
Revolution...

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:06.230
A time for change!

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:08.040
Revolution?

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:12.860
STARISH is doing very well right now.

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:16.290
But an idol must never be satisfied.

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:20.790
He must keep trying, trying, and trying.

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:25.040
I've come up with a plan to help you do that.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:29.420
My plan is...

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:32.520
I call it...

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:35.510
Cross-Unit!

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:40.140
Cross...

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.390
...Unit...

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:47.150
The seven of you will form new units.

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:49.480
Who will be in our groups?

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:51.400
Tell us.

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:56.360
Your Cross-Unit groups will be...

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:07.000
Your groups are...

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:16.340
Give me a minute!

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:09.460
Good grief.

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:12.410
The boss is full of surprises.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:16.890
He sounded just like a Shiba Inu 
when he told us to wait.

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:18.340
Not even close.

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:20.640
Cross-Unit, huh?

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:24.300
You'll be singing in new groups.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:27.220
It's a very interesting idea.

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:28.390
But...

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:34.100
He said we couldn't enter the Triple S.

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:52.210
Revolution.

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:59.260
The seven of us and Nanami-san 
should start a revolution.

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:01.800
STARISH and Haru-chan should start...

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:03.260
...a revolution?

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:06.220
What do you mean?

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:08.100
I see.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.180
The entry deadline is three months from now.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:15.350
We just need to convince 
the president before then.

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:20.360
Yes. The Cross-Units will be 
a good chance to do that.

00:04:20.770 --> 00:04:22.240
I get it.

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:25.360
I'm excited for the Cross-Unit groups now.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:27.490
Let's go all out!

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:29.620
What a wonderful revolution!

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:35.170
I'll do my best to write 
great songs for you, too.

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:52.400
The ocean! It's the ocean!

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:54.150
How exciting!

00:04:56.840 --> 00:04:59.150
What a cute crab.

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:03.280
Aijima, you're going into the water?

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:05.200
I don't like water.

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:08.430
What are they doing?

00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:10.950
We're not here to play.

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:13.480
Icchi, are you trying not to burn?

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:17.110
N-Not really.

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:18.180
Really?

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:23.830
Good morning.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:26.680
Everyone's here.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:32.640
Just so you know, there are 
two purposes for this two-day shoot.

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:38.600
The first is next month's <i>Shining TV! 
Luxurious Resort For Love</i> special!

00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:42.320
We're recording the variety segment for the show.

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:45.980
The other is on next year's calendar.

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:49.070
In between these, you'll be doing 
individual shoots and interviews.

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:52.950
Check your individual schedules.

00:05:55.070 --> 00:05:55.910
Rei-chan.

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:58.290
I look forward to working with you today.

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:02.760
So do I.

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:05.010
By the way, I heard the news.

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:08.590
You went to ask Shining-san 
about entering the Triple S.

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:11.970
Yes, but he turned us down.

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:13.850
You're naïve.

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:16.430
You know it's impossible.

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:18.460
That's harsh.

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:21.310
But you're not giving up, are you?

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:23.490
That's right, Ai-chan.

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:26.690
We'll work together to make it happen.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:31.060
It's obvious based on your past behavior.

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:33.020
That's great.

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:35.660
I like boys who try.

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:37.790
Rei-chan, we'll do our best.

00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:39.510
Enough talk.

00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:40.540
Show us you can do it.

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:58.810
Otoyan and Tokki, show us what you can do.

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:03.250
Hello!

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:04.770
Hello!

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:08.700
Today, Reiji...

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:10.560
...Otoya...

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:12.090
...and Tokiya...

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:16.790
...are going to play with you.

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:24.000
What should we do first?

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:26.210
Should we sing a song?

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:28.630
But then...

00:07:30.890 --> 00:07:33.210
A sudden disaster?!

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:36.970
It's an emergency!

00:07:37.480 --> 00:07:38.850
Calm down, everyone!

00:07:46.050 --> 00:07:50.420
You're so cute that the bee wanted 
to see you from up close.

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:56.830
Bye-bye, bee.

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:58.790
I'm impressed.

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:00.790
Nice hat, right?

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:02.560
It's a magic hat.

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:06.290
Shaking, dancing...

00:08:06.950 --> 00:08:07.540
Woo!

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:11.660
But that's our closing act.

00:08:11.660 --> 00:08:16.570
We need to calm down 
the children and win them over.

00:08:16.570 --> 00:08:17.770
You're right.

00:08:17.770 --> 00:08:19.090
Let's join him.

00:08:19.090 --> 00:08:19.890
Yes.

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:23.390
It's okay.

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:25.740
We have some for everyone.

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:32.880
Here you go.

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:33.950
They're yummy.

00:08:34.350 --> 00:08:36.000
I want a red one!

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:37.200
Me, too!

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:41.080
I like red, too.

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:43.920
Don't push me!

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:45.420
Don't push me!

00:08:45.840 --> 00:08:47.420
Don't fight.

00:08:53.410 --> 00:08:55.510
We're all friends.

00:08:57.830 --> 00:08:58.970
Okay.

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:01.280
Good, good.

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:03.810
Now let's practice singing together.

00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:19.840
The weather's perfect for a walk.

00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:23.600
It's nice to get out of 
the car and walk around.

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:41.430
Ran-chan.

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:44.520
Kurosaki-san, care to share your thoughts?

00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:50.790
Maybe this plan was too much for us.

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:54.580
No, we can make it work.

00:09:57.220 --> 00:10:00.450
What is this indescribable smell?

00:10:01.150 --> 00:10:03.370
Smells like Worcestershire sauce.

00:10:05.670 --> 00:10:06.580
Is it coming from there?

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:11.460
Don't tell me you've never heard of takoyaki.

00:10:12.150 --> 00:10:13.700
I've heard the name.

00:10:14.470 --> 00:10:16.090
I've never eaten them, though.

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:28.430
They're delicious...

00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:36.490
The sauce brings out the flavor 
of the burning hot morsel.

00:10:36.910 --> 00:10:41.950
Despite its name, it contains 
only a tiny bit of octopus.

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:47.170
That amazing dish was very carefully designed.

00:10:47.170 --> 00:10:47.890
Yes.

00:10:53.320 --> 00:10:55.460
Street musicians?

00:10:56.370 --> 00:10:58.010
Looks like it.

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:03.910
Look. It's Kurosaki Ranmaru.

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:17.770
Kurosaki-san.

00:11:17.770 --> 00:11:18.530
Ran-chan.

00:11:19.430 --> 00:11:22.110
I always follow my heart.

00:11:28.530 --> 00:11:29.460
I'll borrow this.

00:11:58.180 --> 00:12:01.230
This wasn't planned, but he's fitting right in.

00:12:01.230 --> 00:12:02.530
I'm not surprised.

00:12:10.180 --> 00:12:12.580
An Aristocratic Afternoon in 
a Beautiful Tea Room

00:12:18.270 --> 00:12:21.530
Fragrant tea and exquisite sweets.

00:12:21.530 --> 00:12:24.150
Perfectly thorough service.

00:12:24.150 --> 00:12:28.470
This place promises to deliver 
a wonderful afternoon.

00:12:28.950 --> 00:12:32.480
<i>Camus becomes another person when he works.</i>

00:12:33.590 --> 00:12:36.470
I hope some beautiful ladies 
will someday join us

00:12:37.250 --> 00:12:40.390
in this tea room full of tradition and elegance.

00:12:41.080 --> 00:12:42.400
Cecil, the sugar.

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:44.120
Yes, sir.

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:01.530
<i>This is how Camus normally behaves.</i>

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:13.510
It's perfect.

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:15.960
What's going on?

00:13:17.640 --> 00:13:20.270
I can't believe we can't 
enter while you're filming.

00:13:20.700 --> 00:13:22.560
I'm terribly sorry.

00:13:22.560 --> 00:13:25.520
We'll let you know once we're finished.

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:29.360
No way! We want to go now!

00:13:29.360 --> 00:13:32.540
Ladies, I'm terribly sorry.

00:13:36.820 --> 00:13:38.540
<i>Camus, what are you...</i>

00:13:42.100 --> 00:13:43.050
Are you...

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:50.220
Please accept my sincerest 
apologies for offending you.

00:13:50.660 --> 00:13:52.360
Actually, we...

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:56.120
I'll have some tea prepared for you.

00:13:56.120 --> 00:13:59.160
Would you like to watch us film?

00:14:01.770 --> 00:14:05.980
I'm delighted to have 
such beautiful ladies watch us.

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:14.290
We'll work as quickly as possible, 
so you can be seated soon.

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:16.740
O-Okay...

00:14:24.640 --> 00:14:27.100
Why are we doing this?

00:14:27.100 --> 00:14:30.690
Couldn't we have done food or marine sports?

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:35.530
Your heart rate is rising, 
and you're starting to sweat.

00:14:35.530 --> 00:14:37.180
You're afraid, Syo.

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:39.460
I-I'm not scared!

00:14:39.460 --> 00:14:40.690
That's right.

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:43.610
Who would be scared?

00:14:44.160 --> 00:14:45.880
We get to meet ghosties.

00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:46.930
What?!

00:14:46.930 --> 00:14:49.070
What are you talking about?

00:14:49.690 --> 00:14:54.530
I made some cookies 
to share with the ghosties.

00:14:54.810 --> 00:14:56.740
Cookies?

00:14:57.400 --> 00:14:59.000
You'll kill the ghosts...

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:02.030
Aren't ghosts already dead?

00:15:02.920 --> 00:15:05.570
Anyway, ghosts don't exist.

00:15:05.570 --> 00:15:07.380
They couldn't be less scientific.

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:10.040
Y-Yeah, you're right.

00:15:11.060 --> 00:15:12.340
There it is.

00:15:24.380 --> 00:15:25.530
What?

00:15:25.940 --> 00:15:28.480
Something feels wrong.

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:30.450
This place gives me chills.

00:15:33.130 --> 00:15:35.180
It's a cute flower.

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:37.490
D-Don't scare me like that!

00:15:38.230 --> 00:15:39.280
I figured it out.

00:15:40.550 --> 00:15:43.340
The twisting path, the shape of this tunnel,

00:15:43.340 --> 00:15:49.880
and the angles and shadows of the 
surrounding trees create a sense of unease.

00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:52.380
They make anyone who looks at them anxious.

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:53.270
What?

00:15:54.560 --> 00:16:01.020
Maybe you're feeling chills 
because cool air collects here.

00:16:01.780 --> 00:16:04.960
I-I see. So that's why.

00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:07.650
Too bad. I brought cookies and everything.

00:16:08.100 --> 00:16:10.200
Man, that's a relief.

00:16:11.290 --> 00:16:12.860
I know. As long as we're here...

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:27.170
I'm so glad you like them.

00:16:28.870 --> 00:16:30.670
Primarily made of flour.

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:33.800
Contains durian, celery, 
dried mackerel, cream.

00:16:34.040 --> 00:16:37.860
There's a pinch of surströmming, too.

00:16:37.860 --> 00:16:40.770
You know everything, Ai-chan.

00:16:41.910 --> 00:16:43.850
How can you be so calm?

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:47.850
Anyway, this is simply a cool place.

00:16:47.850 --> 00:16:49.560
It's great when it's hot out.

00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:53.330
You're already wrapping up?

00:16:53.330 --> 00:16:55.280
You really are amazing.

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:05.920
What a fulfilling day.

00:17:09.600 --> 00:17:11.840
I had a fulfilling day, too.

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:18.240
I wonder if they did, too.

00:17:18.660 --> 00:17:20.640
You mean STARISH?

00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:27.520
Yes. They've never worked 
so closely with QUARTET NIGHT before.

00:17:27.800 --> 00:17:31.030
I'm sure they've learned something.

00:17:31.580 --> 00:17:34.280
Otherwise, they couldn't 
set their sights so high.

00:17:39.110 --> 00:17:40.270
You're right.

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:45.250
Rei-chan was amazing.

00:17:46.010 --> 00:17:49.460
I'm using to taking care of little kids.

00:17:50.200 --> 00:17:52.820
But I couldn't do what he did.

00:17:53.400 --> 00:17:54.420
You're right.

00:17:55.080 --> 00:17:58.230
Kotobuki-san always seems so frantic.

00:17:58.230 --> 00:18:00.570
Well, he really is.

00:18:01.260 --> 00:18:04.810
But he pays attention to his surroundings.

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:08.780
I was impressed by Ran-chan's 
bold professionalism, too.

00:18:09.800 --> 00:18:12.520
Follow your heart, huh?

00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:16.740
Camus' thoughtfulness was incredible.

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:19.280
Ai's calmness was amazing, too.

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:22.200
He did a great job supporting us.

00:18:28.600 --> 00:18:32.340
We still have a lot to learn.

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:33.810
We'd better work harder.

00:18:34.580 --> 00:18:37.110
We must apply ourselves.

00:18:37.110 --> 00:18:39.400
I'm so happy.

00:18:40.810 --> 00:18:44.240
I'm so glad we met.

00:18:46.740 --> 00:18:47.880
You're right.

00:18:48.330 --> 00:18:53.690
We all came to Saotome Academy, were drawn 
to Nanami's music, and formed a group.

00:18:54.260 --> 00:18:57.990
We wouldn't have the same 
sound if anyone were missing.

00:18:57.990 --> 00:19:00.160
I'm grateful we met.

00:19:00.980 --> 00:19:03.530
I feel the same about our seniors.

00:19:03.800 --> 00:19:08.100
Yes. We often lose our way...

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:12.650
But I'm glad we have them to look up to.

00:19:12.650 --> 00:19:14.000
Someday...

00:19:14.380 --> 00:19:17.460
Will we see HEAVENS again someday?

00:19:18.360 --> 00:19:21.420
They've been missing since 
the Uta Pri Award, right?

00:19:21.420 --> 00:19:24.640
The media's been desperately 
searching but can't find them.

00:19:25.150 --> 00:19:27.960
I hope we can sing together again.

00:19:27.960 --> 00:19:29.600
Huh.

00:19:33.210 --> 00:19:35.190
You're really excited about this.

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:38.190
Don't be stupid.

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:42.850
If you really want to enter the Triple S, 
you'll need more than spirit.

00:19:43.460 --> 00:19:45.200
You'll never make it.

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:46.970
We're serious about this.

00:19:47.410 --> 00:19:50.080
We'll change Saotome-san's mind.

00:19:51.780 --> 00:19:54.560
Good, good. Nice expressions.

00:19:54.560 --> 00:19:57.570
Join us on our level.

00:19:58.250 --> 00:20:00.090
If you can, that is.

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:05.600
Let's aim even higher together.

00:21:59.630 --> 00:22:05.910
I will now announce the Cross-Unit groups!

00:22:05.910 --> 00:22:08.010
First...

00:22:08.010 --> 00:22:12.790
Ittoki Otoya... and Shinomiya Natsuki.

00:22:13.220 --> 00:22:16.290
Next are Jinguji Ren,

00:22:16.290 --> 00:22:17.830
Kurusu Syo,

00:22:17.830 --> 00:22:19.440
and Aijima Cecil.

00:22:19.440 --> 00:22:22.670
Finally, Hijirikawa Masato...

00:22:22.670 --> 00:22:25.690
and Ichinose Tokiya.

00:22:25.950 --> 00:22:31.280
Now show me your new charm.

00:24:06.240 --> 00:24:09.330
Don't miss our Love Revolution!

00:24:09.330 --> 00:24:10.720
Uta Pri!
